SUMMARY:TONIGHT | You Can Call Me Paul (A Paul Simon Tribute)
DESCRIPTION:You Can Call Me Paul | May 9\, 2026 7:00 PM | $31+ Event Details and Tickets\n\nBenjamin Falcon formed a love of the Simon & Garfunkel songbook while growing up outside of DC\, in Alexandria\, VA\, through his parents fondness and nostalgia for Simon’s early work\, as well as Falcon’s frequent exposure to the music in radio and media. In college\, Falcon began to explore the larger catalogue of both Simon’s early and solo material.\n\n“You can call me Paul” has since sold out venues and attracted the collaboration of nationally touring musicians of note\, including Jason Hann (The String Cheese Incident)\, Justin Ray (Michael Bublé)\, Justin Stanton (Snarky Puppy).\nThis twelve-member band was assembled to authentically recreate the experience of seeing Simon’s solo work through the eras\, in a live setting\, with all the power and emotion that drew you to start.\n  \nFounded in 2005\, Pisgah is known for producing some of the most sought after craft ales in Western North Carolina. Pisgah Brewing Company currently operates the new indoor taproom & deli\, with live music several days a week\, plus an open air outdoor bar in the summer and fall months. Check out our upcoming schedule at pisgahbrewing.com/events
URL:https://livemusicasheville.com/calendar/you-can-call-me-paul-a-paul-simon-tribute-2/
LOCATION:Pisgah Brewing Company Black Mountain\, 2948 US-70\, Black Mountain\, NC\, 28711
CATEGORIES:Asheville Area,Black Mountain,Live Music
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://livemusicasheville.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/657258735_1413883220765850_5372182365295250927_n-e1774645194201.jpg
GEO:35.6068069;-82.3568213
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Pisgah Brewing Company Black Mountain 2948 US-70 Black Mountain NC 28711;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=2948 US-70:geo:-82.3568213,35.6068069
END:VEVENT
